        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px;">OUR WARRANTY TO YOU...</p>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 15px;"><strong>IMPORTANT NOTICE: Read this entire ETO Doors Limited Warranty and Limitation of Liability ("Limited Warranty") before purchasing or installing this product. By installing or using this product you are acknowledging that this Limited Warranty is part of the terms of sale.</strong><br>
        <em>A Delivery Release must be faxed to ETO within 72 hours of receiving doors to validate warranty.</em></p>

        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px;">WHAT THIS WARRANTY COVERS</p>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">This Limited Warranty applies only to ETO Doors (ETO) wood entry doors, interior doors, door frames, sidelights and transoms ("Covered Products"). ETO makes the following exclusive express Limited Warranties for ETO Wood Door System products installed within the United States and Canada, subject to the stated conditions and limitations. This Limited Warranty is not transferable.</p>

        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">I. Non-glass Materials & Workmanship One-Year (1-Year) Nontransferable Limited Warranty.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">ETO warrants that the non-glass components of its Wood Doors shall be free of manufacturing defects in material or workmanship that significantly impair their proper operation and function for one (1) year from the date of sale. Should the warranted wood door be found to contain defects in materials or workmanship as installed in its original door opening occurring within one (1) year from the date of sale by ETO, ETO shall, and at its sole option: 1) repair or replace: defects, material or workmanship that significantly impairs the proper operation and function or 2) refund the original purchase price. Grilles or any other alterations not installed by ETO may void this warranty. This Limited Warranty on Non-glass Components does not apply to hardware finishes.</p>

        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">II. Non-decorative and Decorative Glass One-Year (1-Year) Limited Warranty.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">ETO warrants that all the glass (clear insulated and decorative insulated) shall be free from premature failure or permanent material obstruction of vision due to a failure of the glass seal for one (1) year from the date of sale by ETO. If ETO is given notice of a glass defect occurring within one (1) year of the date of sale by ETO, ETO shall, at its sole option: 1) repair or replace the defective glass or 2) refund the original purchase price.</p>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;"><strong>NOTE: ETO cannot under any circumstances be responsible for installation, repainting, refinishing or other similar activities necessary to complete the replacement or any cost associated with the resolve of glass claims.</strong></p>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 30px;">ETO will furnish the insulated glass only free of charge, F.O.B. the original point of delivery. Cracked or broken glass is not covered by the warranty. Decorative glass that is hand crafted may vary from one lite to another and contain variations in color, size, glass clarity and welded joints may differ. These are not defects. Tempered glass contains varying degrees of distortions. These distortions may affect view and are not considered a defect. All glass should be cleaned with mild soap & water only. All other solutions could cause damage or seal failure. Do not allow metal parts of cleaning equipment to contact glass.</p>

        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px;">III. Important Notes and Requirements For Your Warranty:</p>
        <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>1. NOTE: EXCEPT AS OTHERWISE EXPRESSLY PROVIDED HEREIN, ETO SHALL NOT PAY FOR THE COST OF LABOR, INSTALLATION, FINISHING, PAINTING, SHIPPING ETC. OF THE REPLACEMENT OF THE ORIGINAL DOOR OR FOR ANY OTHER COST RELATING TO THE REPLACEMENT OF THE DOOR, ALL OF THESE COSTS DESCRIBED SHALL BE THE SOLE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE PERSON MAKING THE WARRANTY CLAIM.</strong></p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>2. NOTE:</strong> Since many minor flaws can be repaired or corrected, all items should be inspected thoroughly for such defects upon receipt and before machining. Please be aware that the machining of a door, sidelight or transom constitutes acceptance of the product as it was received by our customer. Any minor flaws or defects that may exist at the time of machining will not be considered as defective product or claimable once machining has been completed. So, please inspect all items thoroughly before the machining process takes place. These doors are shipped to you unsealed and unfinished, so we do not warrant against the natural characteristics of the wood which may occur in the various conditions encountered from our plant to your finished opening. Because the wood can respond in different ways to the variety of atmospheric and environmental conditions, it is imperative that special attention is given to the door and the necessary care and effort taken to protect the door in the unfinished state to minimize the potential for problems.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>3. NOTE:</strong> Doors must be installed providing protection from exposure, typically with a standard overhang extending outward a distance equal to one-half its height from the bottom of the door up to the overhang to be covered by this warranty.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>4. NOTE:</strong> Any deterioration caused by failure to finish and seal all exposed surfaces and edges of the door within 48 hours of delivery are not covered by this warranty. For continued protection, the finish needs to be maintained yearly.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>5. NOTE:</strong> Please comply with all of the handling and finishing instructions completely to validate the warranty. The product must be hand- sanded before finishing.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>6. NOTE: ETO is not responsible for or makes no warranty as to:</strong> Any visible defect or mistake in shipment reported to ETO Doors <span style="text-decoration: underline;">more than 24 hours after receipt</span> or after the product is machined or installed.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">Without the notation "Potential Damage, Subject To Inspection" on the delivery receipt, ETO doors cannot guarantee reimbursement in case of shipping damage.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>7. NOTE:</strong> All doors must be finished within 48 hours of receiving the door and due to the hygroscopic nature of lumber should not be stored in an unfinished state beyond this period.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>8. NOTE:</strong> Doors must be stored flat on a level surface in a dry, well ventilated building at least 4" above the ground and covered to avoid direct sunlight, as well as moisture, dirt and dust.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>9. NOTE:</strong> ETO may charge a fee for on-site product inspections that will only be reimbursed to the customer if a valid claim under this warranty exists.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>10. NOTE:</strong> DO NOT ATTEMPT TO RETURN ANY ITEMS WITHOUT PRIOR <strong>WRITTEN</strong> AUTHORIZATION FROM ETO DOORS.</p>
        </div>

        <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px;">IV. Important Handling, Finishing and Installation Instructions:</p>
        <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">1. Most finishes on exterior doors deteriorate relatively quickly. To insure exterior doors receive the protection required, inspect the condition of exterior finish at least once a year and refinish as often as needed to maintain the protective stability of the finish.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">2. Entrance doors shall always be shipped and stored vertically (not leaning).</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">3. Doors shall not be exposed to excessive heat, dryness, humidity or direct sunlight prior to finishing.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">4. Handle door with clean gloves and do not drag doors across each other or other surfaces.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">5. If doors are stored on the job site for more than 7 days, all exposed surfaces and edges of the door must be finished and sealed — even if stored out of the elements.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">6. All hardware locations, preparations and methods of installation must be appropriate for the specific door.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">7. All doors 7' and under must have three hinges. Doors over 7' must have four hinges. (Exception: 8' Round Top will have three hinges)</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">8. Prior to finishing, remove all handling marks with 150-grit or finer sandpaper and remove all sanding dust.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">9. Apply sealer, primer or first coat of required finish immediately after fitting, cutting for hardware, etc., and before the installation of hardware.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>10. ALL EXPOSED SURFACES OF THE DOOR MUST BE SEALED, INCLUDING THE TOP, BOTTOM, SIDE EDGES AND THE HARDWARE CUTOUTS.</strong></p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">11. NOTE: An interior-grade lacquer is NOT a satisfactory product for exterior use.</p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">12. All exterior surfaces — including the top, bottom and sides of the door — must be finish coated with a good quality exterior- grade paint or top coat. <strong>(AT LEAST 3 COATS OF EXTERIOR GRADE TOP COAT WITH A UV INHIBITOR MUST BE APPLIED.)</strong></p>
           <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">13. In order not to induce warpage or excessive deterioration of your door, avoid using dark stains or paints on the door surfaces exposed to direct sunlight.</p>
        </div>

